# Full-Universe Data Safety

- Full-universe preprocessing and training MUST be disk-backed and chunked.
- Never accumulate all per-symbol sequence arrays in lists, call a full-universe
  `np.concatenate`, or copy a complete memmap with `.astype()` / TensorFlow
  `from_tensor_slices`.
- Use the `memmap_v1` manifest bundle: read-only `.npy` memmaps, streaming
  scaler statistics, atomic staging/publish, and chunked TensorFlow batches.
- Full runs use `run_preprocessing.py --storage-format memmap` (or `auto` with
  uncapped `--symbol-scope all`). `dev200` and smaller experiments may retain
  compressed NPZ artifacts.
- Before training, verify the manifest/config symbol count and split shapes.
  A filename containing `full` is not proof of universe coverage.
- Never rerun after an OOM without identifying the peak-memory operation and
  changing it. Preserve at least 25% WSL memory headroom.
- Update `ML_Iteration_2/SESSION_HANDOFF.md` whenever the storage contract or
  full-universe operational procedure changes.
